---
// Privacy Policy, as supplied by the hospital (19 November 2026).
// SEO title, description and focus keyword are set below; update "updated" when the text changes.
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import { SITE, digits } from '../config';

const site = 'https://www.chiragglobalhospitals.com/';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  metaTitle="Privacy Policy | Chirag Global Hospitals"
  description="Read the Chirag Global Hospitals Privacy Policy to understand how we collect, use, store and protect your personal information."
  keywords="Chirag Global Hospitals Privacy Policy"
  updated="19 November 2026"
>
  <p>Website: <a href={site}>{site}</a></p>

  <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
  <p>Welcome to {SITE.name} (<a href={site}>{site}</a>).</p>
  <p>
    At {SITE.name}, we respect the privacy of our patients, website visitors and individuals who contact us. We are
    committed to handling personal information responsibly and maintaining the confidentiality of information shared
    with us.
  </p>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, protect and share personal information when you visit our
    website, submit an appointment request or communicate with our hospital.
  </p>
  <p>By accessing or using our website, you acknowledge that you have read this Privacy Policy.</p>

  <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>We may collect personal information when you browse our website, contact our hospital or request an appointment.</p>

  <h3>A. Personal Information</h3>
  <p>Depending on how you interact with our website, we may collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Full name</li>
    <li>Email address</li>
    <li>Mobile or contact number</li>
    <li>Appointment date and preferred time</li>
    <li>Enquiry or message details</li>
    <li>Other information voluntarily provided through website forms or communication channels.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>B. Health-Related Information</h3>
  <p>
    When you contact us regarding medical consultations or treatment, you may voluntarily provide health-related
    information, including:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Symptoms or health concerns</li>
    <li>Medical history</li>
    <li>Previous treatments</li>
    <li>Treatment or consultation enquiries</li>
    <li>Other information relevant to your healthcare requirements.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We handle health-related information with appropriate confidentiality and use it only for relevant healthcare,
    communication and administrative purposes, subject to applicable laws.
  </p>

  <h3>C. Automatically Collected Information</h3>
  <p>When you visit our website, certain technical information may be collected automatically, including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>IP address</li>
    <li>Browser type and version</li>
    <li>Device information</li>
    <li>Operating system</li>
    <li>Pages visited</li>
    <li>Date and time of visits</li>
    <li>Referring website or traffic source.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <p>{SITE.name} may use collected information for the following purposes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to appointment requests and enquiries.</li>
    <li>To schedule and coordinate consultations.</li>
    <li>To communicate information about hospital services and treatments.</li>
    <li>To facilitate communication between patients and authorised hospital representatives.</li>
    <li>To improve website performance and user experience.</li>
    <li>To understand website traffic and visitor behaviour.</li>
    <li>To maintain website security and prevent spam or fraudulent activities.</li>
    <li>To maintain relevant administrative and healthcare records.</li>
    <li>To comply with applicable legal and regulatory requirements.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We process personal information for specified and legitimate purposes in accordance with applicable data protection
    laws.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Appointment Booking and Enquiries</h2>
  <p>
    Our website provides appointment booking facilities through which visitors may submit details such as their name,
    email address, phone number and preferred appointment date and time.
  </p>
  <p>When you submit an appointment request:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your information may be used to contact you regarding your appointment.</li>
    <li>Authorised hospital personnel may access the submitted details to coordinate your consultation.</li>
    <li>Your contact details may be used for appointment confirmations, scheduling changes and related communication.</li>
    <li>Additional information may be requested when necessary to facilitate your consultation.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Submitting an appointment request does not automatically guarantee confirmation of an appointment. The hospital may
    contact you to confirm availability and other details.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
  <p>
    Our website may use cookies and similar technologies to improve website functionality and understand how visitors
    interact with our content.
  </p>
  <p>Cookies may help us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Analyse website traffic and usage.</li>
    <li>Improve website navigation and functionality.</li>
    <li>Understand visitor preferences.</li>
    <li>Monitor website performance.</li>
    <li>Support website security.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can manage or disable cookies through your browser settings.</p>
  <p>
    Where required by applicable law, we will obtain consent before using non-essential cookies and tracking
    technologies.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Google Analytics and Third-Party Tools</h2>
  <p>
    We may use third-party services, such as Google Analytics, to analyse website traffic and understand visitor
    interactions.
  </p>
  <p>
    These services may collect technical and usage-related information, including pages visited, session duration,
    device information, browser details and traffic sources.
  </p>
  <p>Third-party services process information according to their respective privacy policies.</p>
  <p>
    For more information about Google's privacy practices, visit:
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>
  </p>

  <h2>7. WhatsApp and Other Communication Channels</h2>
  <p>Our website may provide communication options such as WhatsApp, telephone calls and email.</p>
  <p>If you choose to contact us through these channels:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>We may receive your contact details and the information you voluntarily share.</li>
    <li>Your information may be used to respond to your enquiry or coordinate an appointment.</li>
    <li>Communication through third-party platforms is also subject to the privacy policies and terms of those platforms.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We encourage visitors to avoid sharing unnecessary sensitive medical information through unsecured communication
    channels.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Sharing of Personal Information</h2>
  <p>{SITE.name} does not sell personal information to third parties.</p>
  <p>We may share personal information in limited circumstances, including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Authorised Hospital Personnel:</strong> With authorised employees and healthcare professionals who require
      the information to provide healthcare services or respond to enquiries.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Service Providers:</strong> With trusted third-party providers involved in website hosting, maintenance,
      security, analytics, appointment management or communication services.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Healthcare Coordination:</strong> Where necessary for consultations, treatment coordination, referrals or
      other relevant healthcare activities, subject to applicable confidentiality requirements.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal Requirements:</strong> When disclosure is required by applicable law, court orders, regulatory
      authorities or lawful government requests.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We take reasonable steps to ensure that personal information shared with service providers is handled appropriately.</p>

  <h2>9. Data Security and Patient Confidentiality</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal information against unauthorised
    access, misuse, disclosure, alteration or loss.
  </p>
  <p>
    Access to personal information is intended to be limited to authorised individuals who require it for relevant
    operational or healthcare purposes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Patient information and medical records are handled with appropriate confidentiality, subject to applicable legal and
    professional requirements.
  </p>
  <p>However, no electronic storage or internet transmission method can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>

  <h2>10. Data Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary to fulfil the purposes for which it was
    collected, including:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Responding to enquiries.</li>
    <li>Managing appointment requests.</li>
    <li>Providing healthcare services.</li>
    <li>Maintaining relevant administrative and medical records.</li>
    <li>Meeting applicable legal and regulatory obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Medical records may be retained in accordance with applicable healthcare and record-retention requirements.</p>
  <p>
    When personal information is no longer required, we will take reasonable steps to securely delete or dispose of it,
    subject to applicable legal obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
  <p>Subject to applicable data protection laws, you may have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Request access to your personal information.</li>
    <li>Request correction or updating of inaccurate information.</li>
    <li>Request deletion of personal information where legally permitted.</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
    <li>Raise concerns regarding the handling of your personal information.</li>
    <li>Submit a privacy-related grievance through our contact details.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We will review and respond to requests in accordance with applicable legal requirements.</p>

  <h2>12. External Website Links</h2>
  <p>Our website may contain links to external websites, social media platforms or third-party resources.</p>
  <p>
    These external websites operate independently and may follow different privacy policies and data collection
    practices.
  </p>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is not responsible for the privacy practices, content or security of third-party websites. We recommend
    reviewing their privacy policies before sharing personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Where personal information relating to children is collected in connection with healthcare services, we will handle
    such information in accordance with applicable laws and obtain verifiable parental or guardian consent where
    required.
  </p>
  <p>We take appropriate care when handling information relating to children and their healthcare requirements.</p>

  <h2>14. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect changes in our website, hospital services, technology or
    applicable legal requirements.
  </p>
  <p>Any updates will be published on this page with a revised Last Updated date.</p>
  <p>Visitors are encouraged to review this policy periodically.</p>

  <h2>15. Contact Us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions, concerns or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or the handling of your personal
    information, please contact us:
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>{SITE.name}</strong><br />
    Address: 103, 6th Cross Road, Dollar Layout, BTM 2nd Stage, Bengaluru, Karnataka – 560076, India.<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a><br />
    Phone: <a href="tel:08065916422">08065916422</a><br />
    Emergency Contact: <a href={`tel:${digits(SITE.emergency)}`}>{SITE.emergency}</a><br />
    Website: <a href={site}>{site}</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    We will make reasonable efforts to address privacy-related enquiries and grievances in accordance with applicable
    laws.
  </p>

  <hr class="my-10 border-brand-100" />
  <p>
    By using the {SITE.name} website, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
